    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d457">

                <pb facs="0475" n="1209" sameAs="frus:frus1895p2/pg1209"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Olney to Mr. Dupuy de Lôme.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of state</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1896-01-26"><hi rendition="#italic">January 26,
                        1896</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have yours of this date and have sent a
                    copy to the Secretary of the Treasury, Secretary of the Navy, and the
                    Attorney-General, expressing the hope that any attempted violation of the
                    international obligations of the United States would be prevented.</p>
                <p>I have also said that you would furnish each of them with the evidence, or
                    sources of evidence, justifying the statement contained in your letter.</p>
                <p>Begging you to accept the assurances of my highest consideration,</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Richard Olney.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
